="CHROMIUM: arm64: tegra: smaug: Update PMIC settings to ensure power down sequence  This patch includes the fixes below. * Set TFPS0 and TFPS1 to 5.12mS. This is required to ensure that 1.8V   rails decay prior to RTC turn off in power down sequence. * Move RTC and SoC rail to slot 7. * Move DRAM-1.1V to slot 1. * Move 1.8V to slot 3. * Move 3.3V to slot 2.  CQ-DEPEND=CL:308950 BUG=chrome-os-partner:46124,chrome-os-partner:46608 TEST=cold boot and suspend/resume stress test  Change-Id: I49884dc25f3f18324735a1b5a4bb37f5f66a300d Signed-off-by: Joseph Lo &lt;josephl@nvidia.com&gt; Signed-off-by: Andrew Bresticker &lt;abrestic@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/308619 Reviewed-by: Benson Leung &lt;bleung@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="308619" owner_email="abrestic@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/19/308619/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="I9624dda5cfc5b5d208992b5b3ba1aaf278faf2cf" commit="2e81b3c781034e06e501496728e4f6ddf3b09b9b" commit_message="CHROMIUM: arm64: tegra: smaug: Adjust PWRGOOD and PWROFF timer values  We need to extend the PWROFF, PWRGOOD, and OSC_POSTPWR timers to account for the changes in the MAX77620 suspend/resume power sequence.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:46124,chrome-os-partner:46608 TEST=LP0 suspend/resume test  Change-Id: I9624dda5cfc5b5d208992b5b3ba1aaf278faf2cf Signed-off-by: Joseph Lo &lt;josephl@nvidia.com&gt; Signed-off-by: Andrew Bresticker &lt;abrestic@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/308950 Reviewed-by: Benson Leung &lt;bleung@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="308950" owner_email="abrestic@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/50/308950/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-2015.07" change_id="I081623bbb1b0f39f1569b9f5cf7933abefe202b3" commit="3c52bc52f39dbfbadb6eca16e741c73f9939db12" commit_message="glados: Set the type-c flex port to max USB2 settings  Change the tuning setting for the type-c port that is over the flex cable to use the max possible drive strength.  Also fix up the comments to indicate what Type-c port goes where instead of just referring to them by number.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:45367 BRANCH=none TEST=build and boot on glados  Change-Id: I081623bbb1b0f39f1569b9f5cf7933abefe202b3 Signed-off-by: Duncan Laurie &lt;dlaurie@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/309010 Reviewed-by: Aaron Durbin &lt;adurbin@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="309010" owner_email="dlaurie@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/coreboot" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/coreboot" ref="refs/changes/10/309010/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I1eec63e2c59ed143531f2ccabcf76bdcfb125508" commit="fe8ee7aea2729756b869d3110e3f20b296487037" commit_message="overlord: dashboard: fix UI hang by making loadProperties async  Current implementation loads properties from server synchronously, which block UI when refreshing. We now make the loading async, and also remove the 60 second refresh to improve user experience.  BUG=chromium:443972 TEST=manually  Change-Id: I1eec63e2c59ed143531f2ccabcf76bdcfb125508 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/309093 Commit-Ready: Wei-Ning Huang &lt;wnhuang@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Wei-Ning Huang &lt;wnhuang@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Wei-Han Chen &lt;stimim@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="309093" owner_email="wnhuang@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="7" project="chromiumos/platform/factory" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/factory" ref="refs/changes/93/309093/7" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="I800e15c0b10cb371a32dd427d7af2a46ea6292a5" commit="75c7d98e90895aa1c09c7bcfb953d1694fdbce0d" commit_message="CHROMIUM: drm/nouveau: add per channel fifo mutex  The mutex inside nouveau_cli is vastly abused in concurrent access control.  Any operation from the same process will be blocked on the same mutex.  This lazy protection impose a rather low cap on multi- channel performance.  We have seen cases where pushbuf worker thread got delayed on that mutex for more than 100ms just waiting to submit pushbuf to GPU, not counting delay on the same mutex when pushbuf was queued through nouveau_gem_ioctl_pushbuf_2().  While ideal solution is to factorize the mutex into multiple components, leaving only nouveau_abi16 and nouveau_cli under its protection, such refactoring would be huge and of high risk.  Thus we only release the most performance critical part, pushbuf submit, from the control of this mutex.  Further refactoring should be considered depending on performance outcome.  Functions with fifo access (Need to hold chan-&gt;fifo_lock when calling): - nouveau_fence_new() - nouveau_fence_emit() - nouveau_fence_emit_initted() - nouveau_dma_wait() - nv50_dma_*() - nv*_bo_move_*() - BEGIN_*() - OUT_RING() - FIRE_RING() - WIND_RING()  Utility functions already acquire fifo_lock on their own as needed: - nouveau_fence_sync() - nouveau_bo_sync()  BUG=chrome-os-partner:46741 TEST=Run monkey test for camera on smuag, no fence timeout.  Change-Id: I800e15c0b10cb371a32dd427d7af2a46ea6292a5 Signed-off-by: Xia Yang &lt;xiay@nvidia.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/307949 Reviewed-by: David Ung &lt;davidu@nvidia.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Haixia Shi &lt;hshi@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Stéphane Marchesin &lt;marcheu@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="307949" owner_email="xiay@nvidia.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="9" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/49/307949/9" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.14" change_id="I0aae4d01753f041d19c64f76ebae88b9d94db9de" commit="67747025ea4bdf355efd99360544cd5f22edace4" commit_message="FROMLIST: usb: dwc2: host: Fix remote wakeup when not in DWC2_L2  In commit 734643dfbdde (&quot;usb: dwc2: host: add flag to reflect bus state&quot;) we changed dwc2_port_suspend() not to set the lx_state anymore (instead it sets the new bus_suspended variable).  This introduced a bug where we would fail to detect device insertions if:  1. Plug empty hub into dwc2 2. Plug USB flash drive into the empty hub. 3. Wait a few seconds 4. Unplug USB flash drive 5. Less than 2 seconds after step 4, plug the USB flash drive in again.  The dwc2_hcd_rem_wakeup() function should have been changed to look at the new bus_suspended variable.  Let's fix it.  Since commit b46146d59fda (&quot;usb: dwc2: host: resume root hub on remote wakeup&quot;) talks about needing the root hub resumed if the bus was suspended, we'll include it in our test.  It appears that the &quot;port_l1_change&quot; should only be set to 1 if we were in DWC2_L1 (the driver currently never sets this), so we'll update the former &quot;else&quot; case based on this test.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:46812 TEST=see bug  Change-Id: I0aae4d01753f041d19c64f76ebae88b9d94db9de Fixes: 734643dfbdde (&quot;usb: dwc2: host: add flag to reflect bus state&quot;) Signed-off-by: Douglas Anderson &lt;dianders@chromium.org&gt; (am from https://patchwork.kernel.org/patch/7467511/) Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/308181 Reviewed-by: Julius Werner &lt;jwerner@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="308181" owner_email="dianders@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/81/308181/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I6da806245faacf9d305dc226fc11f6da19ae2391" commit="a8497fabdd2e1b1fdd25560c0d0f77f260dead31" commit_message="common-mk: platform2_test: pass through gcov environment variables  This CL adds gcov environment variables to the platform2_test passthrough list for specifying the output location of unit test coverage data.  BUG=None TEST=Manually verify that environment variables are passed to QEMU  Change-Id: I6da806245faacf9d305dc226fc11f6da19ae2391 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/308970 Commit-Ready: Timothy Jennison &lt;tjennison@google.com&gt; Tested-by: Timothy Jennison &lt;tjennison@google.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Mike Frysinger &lt;vapier@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="308970" owner_email="tjennison@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/platform2" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform2" ref="refs/changes/70/308970/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="I9819c4b95876f697e75b1b84810b6c520d9c33ec" commit="74b6cfff24834eb6fe4ab8f5728e16f6a8e5e75f" commit_message="CHROMIUM: android: binder: Fix potential scheduling-while-atomic  Commit f1e7f0a724f6 (&quot;android: binder: Disable preemption while holding the global binder lock.&quot;) re-enabled preemption around most of the sites where calls to potentially sleeping functions were made, but missed __alloc_fd(), which can sleep if the fdtable needs to be resized. Re-enable preemption around __alloc_fd() as well as __fd_install() which can now sleep in upstream kernels as of commit 8a81252b774b (&quot;fs/file.c: don't acquire files-&gt;file_lock in fd_install()&quot;).  BUG=chrome-os-partner:44012 TEST=Build and boot on Smaug.  Change-Id: I9819c4b95876f697e75b1b84810b6c520d9c33ec Signed-off-by: Andrew Bresticker &lt;abrestic@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/308582 Reviewed-by: Stephen Barber &lt;smbarber@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Riley Andrews &lt;riandrews@google.com&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="308582" owner_email="abrestic@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/82/308582/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="If5757377f0e59c484d540637230811d584b14e40" commit="4f5216156716fc65a2343e605af860e434c4b725" commit_message="chell/lars: Add override for JTAG to UART for USBPD  Enable access to USBPD on chell/lars boards.  Re-structure the placement in this file to collect all the sklake boards in the same place.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:46289 TEST=successfully run &quot;flash_ec --board=chell_pd&quot;  Change-Id: If5757377f0e59c484d540637230811d584b14e40 Signed-off-by: Duncan Laurie &lt;dlaurie@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/308747 Reviewed-by: Todd Broch &lt;tbroch@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="308747" owner_email="dlaurie@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/hdctools" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/hdctools" ref="refs/changes/47/308747/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><lkgm version="7587.0.0-rc1"/></manifest>